{
  "id": "perceptual-rivalry",
  "term": "perceptual rivalry",
  "definition": "Perceptual rivalry is a visual phenomenon in which the same input to both eyes leads awareness to alternate between different, mutually exclusive interpretations of what is being seen. It is studied with ambiguous images, such as the Necker cube, whose appearance switches between possible organizations even though the stimulus itself does not change.",
